.TH "PB-CONFIG-LOCAL-ACCESS-DOMAIN-SET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-local-access-domain-set - Set and apply the local browser domain


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config local-access domain set <domain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the browser domain for this local installation. Paperboat validates its DNS scope, provisions the matching local trust, updates the running helper, and persists the setting only through the standard apply workflow.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-local-access-domain(1)\fP
